# gitleaks findings that are not credentials, one fingerprint per line.
#
# The fingerprint is `commit:path:rule:line`, which is the narrowest suppression gitleaks
# offers: it exempts ONE line of ONE file as introduced by ONE commit under ONE rule. A
# `[allowlist] paths` regex would exempt a whole directory forever, and a real key committed
# to that directory tomorrow would scan clean. Nothing here can do that -- edit the line and
# the fingerprint changes, and the scan goes red again.
#
# 1. `ghp_0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzA` is the sequential-alphabet placeholder in
#    Phase 5's plan, inside a test asserting that the evidence redactor MASKS a GitHub token.
#    The document has to contain a token-shaped string in order to specify redacting one.
#    It has never been a credential: the body is `0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz`.
